<title>NIGERIA: Born-again Nigerian returns stolen goods.</title>
<headline>Born-again Nigerian returns stolen goods.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A receiver of stolen goods handed back spare parts worth millions of naira (thousands of dollars) to Nigeria Airways after conversion to Christianity, the National Concord newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The national carrier received the goods on January 15 and is making no comment as it agreed with the repentant businessman that he would be protected for changing his ways, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The man said that he bought the items from thieves before he became a born-again Christian in December.</p>
</text>
